                          Hands-free conversation (mic + TTS); status = readiness
                          Mic missing → soft-fail + hint; use --text without mic
  talk ["prompt"]         Alias for voice (optional one-shot prompt)
  say "message"           Speak a line out loud via Bolt_Voice
  briefing --speak        Generate daily briefing and speak a short summary
  storage [monitor|rotate|optimize|status]
                          Disk + media folder health (fixed paths under media/)
                          status=sizes + sites/cron readiness (advisory);
                          monitor=alerts; rotate/optimize=cleanup
  budget | api-usage      xAI spend this month, soft cap, budget mode
  day [--decide|--voice|--quiet|--open|--process]
                          Morning kickoff; --decide → queue decide (default offer on TTY)
  week [show|set|done|paper|rotate|ban]
                          This week / last week / do not suggest (read before any plan)
                          paper [--open]  one-page fridge sheet (goal + checkboxes)
  vault [status|list|find|add|undo]
                          Obsidian vault (BOLT_VAULT_PATH). Safe writes, backups,
                          activity log. Never deletes. add writes a task note.
  monday [status|sync|watch]
                          Phone board on monday.com. Syncs tasks, events, and
                          pages with the vault when MONDAY_API_TOKEN is set.
                          sync --dry-run shows the plan. Off when the token is empty.
  checkin [--questions|--json|--answer KEY=TEXT]
                          Evening check-in: up to 3 questions on what's not logged
  stats [status|sync|tiktok|youtube] [--dry-run] [--json] [--probe]
                          Social performance pull readiness + TikTok/YouTube sync
  analytics [--days N] [--top N]
                          Summarize clip performance from Data/performance_outcomes.jsonl
  anomaly latest [--game NAME] [--no-save|--dry-run] [--z N] [--json]
                          anomaly media/Recordings/FILE.mkv
                          Score a recording vs historical audio baseline (Anomaly_Detector)
                          (aliases: anomalies, anomaly-detect)
  predict --game G --trigger T [--platform P] [--days N] [--json]
                          Forecast 24h views from performance_outcomes.jsonl
  predict --queue [--limit N] [--days N] [--json]
                          Predict for ready queue clips (Peak_Hour_Notifier insight)
                          (aliases: forecast, views-predict)
  multi [status|plan|show|publish] …
                          Multi-platform plans + honest auto-upload soft-fail
                          (Kick/IG unavailable:; Data/multi_platform_queue.json)
                          (aliases: platforms, multi-publish)
  buffer [status|flush|approve]  Product-cut Buffer schedule (PARTIAL)
                          status shows Data/configs/buffer_product_posting.json
                          approve "Name" --video PATH  (no second confirmation)
                          Missing BUFFER_ACCESS_TOKEN queues the job honestly
  enhance [--dry-run] [--limit N]
                          Smart_Trim → Text_Overlay on media/vertical_clips/
                          (aliases: enhance_clips, smart_trim)
  checkup [--open] [--json]
                          Refresh Data/Bolt_data.js + show App/Bolt_Checkup.html
                          (aliases: dashboard, checkup-dashboard)
  menubar                 Start the macOS menu bar app (App/app.py; needs rumps)
                          (aliases: menu-bar, menu_bar). Install: uv sync --extra menubar
  ocr <clip> [--verbose]  Extract on-screen game-stat text via Video_Intelligence
                          (aliases: video-ocr, extract-stats). Needs pytesseract + tesseract.
  amazon <ASIN|URL> […] [--focus …] [--platform tiktok] [--fetch-only] [--json]
                          Amazon product fetch + review plan (Amazon_Analyzer)
                          (aliases: amazon-review, review-plan). Same path as
                          bolt recordings --content-type review.
  search "question" [--raw|--long|--json] [--limit N]
                          Live DuckDuckGo web search (+ optional LLM summary)
                          (aliases: web-search, websearch). Powers !Bolt chat search.
  word [status|list|define|spell|syn|ant|check] [word]
                          Dictionary / spellcheck / thesaurus (READY)
                          status [--json|--probe]; list; word → full card
                          local spell (/usr/share/dict/words + Data/word_extras.txt)
                          define/syn: free no-key APIs (soft-fail)
                          aliases: dict, dictionary, define, spell, spellcheck,
                          thesaurus, synonym. Distinct from bolt search.
                          Unknown commands hear-through typos (safe ones auto-run).
  overlay [--port 8766]   OBS overlay server (Stream Deck kill/win + cam frame)
  review [--port 8767] [--no-open]
                          Local clip review board (keep / toss). Keep never posts.

Direction-finding researcher (Core/modules/Researcher.py):
  research [status|questions|candidates|pending|log|add|note|c5|find]
                          Profile-aware research role (C5/C6/C7 gates + log)
                          pending --decide  answer every C5 in one pass
                          c5 keep|drop "Name"  — record your C5 decision
                          add "Name" --platform … --summary … --why …
                          find [query] [--dry-run]  — web search → pending C5

Creator Command Center (Core/modules/Command_Center.py):
  mission [status|checkin|playbook|list|show|start|fill|update|next]
                          Turn a goal into a printable mission briefing
                          fill latest   rebuild empty sections from evidence
                          update latest --hours … --budget … --assets …
  command-center …        Alias for mission
  ccc …                   Short alias for mission

Post queue / peak posting (Core/modules/Peak_Hour_Notifier.py):
  queue [status|list|next|decide|clean|approve|buffer|…]
                          Ready-to-post queue (Data/ready_to_post.json)
                          NOT media/vertical_clips/ — that folder is videos only
                          queue buffer           Buffer jobs for approved product cuts
                          queue add FILE --product "Name" --approve
                                              Product cut → Buffer, no second yes
  queue decide            Interactive: open / approve / hold / post (easiest)
  queue next [--open]     Show next postable clip card
  queue package [id]      Manual upload package (paste-ready captions)
  queue clean             Clear ghost rows (ready but file missing)
  approve [clip_id]       Approve next (or named) clip for peak auto-post
  postnow [clip_id]       Publish immediately (alias: post-now)
  mark-posted [clip_id]   After manual upload (alias: queue mark-posted)
  dontpost [clip_id] <why>
                          Hold a clip and record the reason
  tiktok-post [--demo|--live]
                          Compliant Post-to-TikTok web UI (audit demo)
  tiktok-post status      Token / API readiness (no server; demo is valid)
                          (aliases: post-ui, tiktok_post, tiktok-ui)

Built-in subcommands (not script passthroughs):
  setup                   Finite setup check (config + keys); exits when done
  launch                  Start live mode (folder watch + optional OBS)
  test [testmodule]       Run the full test suite (or a specific test module)
  help                    Show this message
  version                 Show Bolt's repo path and Python version

Setup:
  Add to your shell rc (so you can just type 'bolt <thing>'):
    alias bolt='/Users/carter/developer/Bolt/.venv/bin/bolt'
"""


# Posting / notify — suggest on typo, never auto-run from a misspelling.
_CLI_DANGEROUS = frozenset(
    {
        "postnow",
        "post-now",
        "approve",
        "send",
        "notify",
        "dontpost",
        "dont-post",
        "hold-clip",
        "mark-posted",
        "markposted",
        "publish",
    }
)

_TYPO_GUARD = False


def _all_cli_names() -> list[str]:
    """Names Bolt actually answers to (scripts + builtins + help harvest)."""
    names = set(SUBCOMMANDS)
    names.update(MANAGER_COMMANDS)
    names.update(
        {
            "help",
            "version",
            "launch",
            "test",
            "setup",
            "day",
            "today",
            "week",
            "vault",
            "checkin",
            "voice",
            "talk",
            "say", "-v", (os.getenv("Bolt_VOICE") or os.getenv("BOLT_VOICE") or "Nathan (Enhanced)"),
            "queue",
            "approve",
            "postnow",
            "post-now",
            "dontpost",
            "analytics",
            "anomaly",
            "predict",
            "multi",
            "buffer",
            "ocr",
            "amazon",
            "search",
            "word",
            "dict",
            "spell",
            "thesaurus",
            "mission",
            "research",
            "budget",
            "storage",
            "menubar",
            "checkup",
            "enhance",
            "doctor",
            "verify",
        }
    )
    for line in HELP_TEXT.splitlines():
        stripped = line.strip()
        if not stripped:
            continue
        token = stripped.split()[0].strip("`\"'")
        folded = token.replace("-", "").replace("_", "")
        if (
            token
            and token[0].isalpha()
            and token == token.lower()
            and folded.isalnum()
        ):
            names.add(token)
    return sorted(names)


def _closest_command(token: str, names: list[str]) -> list[tuple[str, int]]:
    try:
        if str(CORE_DIR) not in sys.path:
            sys.path.insert(0, str(CORE_DIR))
        from importlib import import_module

        closest_in = import_module("modules.Word_Lookup").closest_in

        return list(closest_in(token, names, limit=4, max_dist=2) or [])
    except Exception:
        return []


def _resolve_unknown_subcommand(token: str) -> tuple[str | None, list[str]]:
    """Unique safe match → (name, suggestions). Else (None, suggestions)."""
    raw = (token or "").strip()
    if not raw:
        return None, []
    names = _all_cli_names()
    folded = raw.lower().replace("_", "").replace("-", "")
    if len(folded) >= 4:
        prefixes: list[str] = []
        seen: set[str] = set()
        for name in names:
            nf = name.replace("_", "").replace("-", "")
            if nf.startswith(folded):
                key = name.replace("_", "-")
                if key not in seen:
                    seen.add(key)
                    prefixes.append(name)
        if len(prefixes) == 1:
            return prefixes[0], prefixes
        if len(prefixes) > 1:
            return None, prefixes[:4]
    hits = _closest_command(raw, names)
    if not hits:
        return None, []
    suggestions = [name for name, _dist in hits]
    best, dist = hits[0]
    unique = len(hits) == 1 or hits[1][1] > dist
    if (
        unique
        and dist <= 2
        and best.lower() not in _CLI_DANGEROUS
        and not (dist == 2 and len(folded) < 6)
    ):
        return best, suggestions
    return None, suggestions


def find_script(name: str) -> Path | None:
    """Look up a subcommand name in SUBCOMMANDS. Return the absolute path
    to the script file, or None if the subcommand isn't a known script.

    Entries starting with "modules/" resolve under Core/ (e.g. Core/modules/X.py);
    everything else resolves under scripts/.
    """
    if name in SUBCOMMANDS:
        rel = SUBCOMMANDS[name]
        base = CORE_DIR if rel.startswith("modules/") else SCRIPTS_DIR
        return base / rel
    return None


def main() -> int:
    args = sys.argv[1:]

    if not args or args[0] in ("-h", "--help", "help"):
        print(HELP_TEXT)
        return 0

    if args[0] in ("-V", "--version", "version"):
        print(f"bolt {REPO_ROOT}")
        print(f"  python  {sys.executable}")
        print(f"  venv    {VENV_PYTHON}  ({'exists' if VENV_PYTHON.exists() else 'NOT FOUND'})")
        return 0

    subcommand, *rest = args
    py = str(VENV_PYTHON if VENV_PYTHON.exists() else sys.executable)

    # Built-in: launch
    if subcommand == "launch":
        cmd = [py, "Core/launch.py"] + rest
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT))

    # Built-in: test
    if subcommand == "test":
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}:{SCRIPTS_DIR.parent}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        test_args = rest if rest else ["discover", "-s", "Data/tests", "-t", "."]
        cmd = [py, "-m", "unittest"] + test_args
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    # Built-in: setup — finite wizard/check pass. Does NOT start live watch.
    # (Historically this handed off to bot.py and looked like a hang forever.)
    if subcommand == "setup":
        cmd = [py, "Core/launch.py", "setup"] + rest
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT))

    # Built-in: daily content kickoff (optionally → queue decide / voice)
    if subcommand in ("week", "this-week", "this_week", "week-card"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        cmd = [py, "-m", "modules.Week_Card"] + rest
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    if subcommand in ("vault", "obsidian", "obsidian-vault"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        cmd = [py, "-m", "modules.Vault_Store"] + (rest if rest else ["status"])
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    if subcommand in ("monday", "monday-sync", "monday_sync"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        cmd = [py, "-m", "modules.Monday_Sync"] + (rest if rest else ["status"])
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    # Built-in: evening check-in (asks what's missing, saves answers locally)
    if subcommand in ("checkin", "check-in", "evening", "evening-checkin"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        cmd = [py, "-m", "modules.Evening_Checkin"] + rest
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    if subcommand in ("day", "today", "kickoff", "start-day", "morning-flow"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        cmd = [py, str(CORE_DIR / "bolt_day.py")] + rest
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    # Built-in: social stats status + TikTok/YouTube performance sync
    if subcommand in ("stats", "social-stats", "social_stats", "performance-sync"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        cmd = [py, "-m", "modules.Social_Stats"] + (rest if rest else ["status"])
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    # Built-in: API budget / usage (soft cap + xai_usage.jsonl)
    if subcommand in ("budget", "api-usage", "api_usage", "xai-usage", "llm-budget"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        do_test = "--test-alert" in rest or "--test" in rest
        # Pass flag into -c script via env (inner python argv is only -c)
        env["BOLT_BUDGET_TEST_ALERT"] = "1" if do_test else "0"
        script = r'''
from modules.LLM_Budget import describe_policy, llm_mode, briefing_provider_preference
from modules.XAI_Usage import status_dict, monthly_cap_usd
from modules.Bolt_Alerts import channels_status
import json, os
print("Bolt LLM / xAI budget")
print("─" * 40)
print(describe_policy())
print(f"mode:              {llm_mode()}")
print(f"briefing provider: {briefing_provider_preference()}")
print(f"monthly cap USD:   {monthly_cap_usd() or 'unlimited'}")
print()
print(json.dumps(status_dict(), indent=2))
print()
print("Alert channels (no Discord):")
print(json.dumps(channels_status(), indent=2))
if os.getenv("BOLT_BUDGET_TEST_ALERT") == "1":
    from modules.Bolt_Alerts import notify
    print()
    print("Sending test alert (Mac + SMS + email)…")
    result = notify(
        "Bolt budget alert test — if you got this, SMS/email/Mac are working.",
        title="Bolt test",
        subject="Bolt alert test",
        email_body=(
            "Bolt budget alert test.\n\n"
            "If you see this email, SMTP is working.\n"
            "SMS uses the same path via your carrier gateway.\n"
        ),
    )
    print("Results:", result)
    if not result.get("email") or not result.get("sms"):
        print(
            "Tip: check Gmail → Sent and Spam. "
            "For SMS, AT&T can delay 1–5 min; ensure SMTP App Password is correct."
        )
'''
        cmd = [py, "-c", script]
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    # Built-in: voice / talk / say — hands-free listen → interpret → speak
    if subcommand in ("voice", "talk", "live-voice", "live_voice", "say"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        if subcommand == "say":
            voice_args = ["--say"] + rest
        else:
            voice_args = list(rest)
        cmd = [py, str(CORE_DIR / "bolt_live_voice.py")] + voice_args
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    # Built-in: sites / storage-cron readiness (local write + scripts + crontab advisory)
    if subcommand in (
        "sites",
        "site-status",
        "sites-status",
        "storage-cron",
        "storage_cron",
    ) or (
        subcommand == "site"
        and (
            (
                [a for a in rest if not a.startswith("-")]
                and [a for a in rest if not a.startswith("-")][0].lower()
                in ("status", "check", "ready")
            )
            or (
                rest
                and not any(a in ("--push", "--path") for a in rest)
                and all(a in ("--json", "--probe") for a in rest)
            )
        )
    ):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        site_args = list(rest)
        if subcommand in (
            "site-status",
            "sites-status",
            "storage-cron",
            "storage_cron",
        ) and not site_args:
            site_args = ["status"]
        # Flag-only --json/--probe → status verb for Sites_Storage
        if site_args and all(a.startswith("-") for a in site_args):
            site_args = ["status"] + site_args
        if not site_args:
            site_args = ["status"]
        cmd = [py, "-m", "modules.Sites_Storage"] + site_args
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)

    # Built-in: storage monitor / rotation / optimization (canonical media/ paths)
    if subcommand in ("storage", "disk", "media-rotation", "storage-monitor"):
        action = rest[0] if rest else "status"
        extra = rest[1:] if rest else []
        os.chdir(REPO_ROOT)
        if action in ("status", "report", "sizes"):
            # Quick sizes-only report (no auto-clean, no notifications)
            script = f'''
from pathlib import Path
import shutil
root = Path({str(REPO_ROOT)!r})
media = root / "media"
for name in ("Recordings", "clips", "vertical_clips", "output"):
    p = media / name
    if not p.exists():
        print(f"  {{name}}: missing ({{p}})")
        continue
    total = sum(f.stat().st_size for f in p.rglob("*") if f.is_file())
    print(f"  {{name}}: {{total/1024**3:.2f}}GB  ({{p}})")
u = shutil.disk_usage(root)
print(f"  Disk: {{100*u.used/u.total:.0f}}% used, {{u.free/1024**3:.1f}}GB free")
'''
            cmd = [py, "-c", script]
            rc = subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT))
            # Sites / storage cron readiness (advisory; soft-fail)
            env = os.environ.copy()
            env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
                f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
            )
            sites_summary = """
try:
    from modules.Sites_Storage import print_status
    print_status(as_json=False, probe=False)
except Exception as exc:
    print(f\"  (sites/storage cron status skipped: {exc})\")
"""
            subprocess.call([py, "-c", sites_summary], cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)
            # Speak a short storage line when auto-speak is on
            speak_script = '''
try:
    from modules.Intent_Router import _action_storage
    from modules.Bolt_Voice import speak_result
    speak_result(_action_storage())
except Exception:
    pass
'''
            subprocess.call([py, "-c", speak_script], cwd=str(REPO_ROOT), env=env)
            return rc
        if action in ("monitor", "check"):
            cmd = ["bash", str(SCRIPTS_DIR / "storage_monitor.sh")] + extra
            return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT))
        if action in ("rotate", "rotation"):
            cmd = ["bash", str(SCRIPTS_DIR / "media_rotation.sh")] + (extra or ["--dry-run"])
            return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT))
        if action in ("optimize", "optimisation", "cleanup"):
            cmd = ["bash", str(SCRIPTS_DIR / "storage_optimization.sh")] + (
                extra or ["--dry-run", "--skip-dedup", "--skip-compress"]
            )
            return subprocess.call(cmd, cwd=str(REPO_ROOT))
        print(f"bolt storage: unknown action '{action}'", file=sys.stderr)
        print("  Use: status | monitor | rotate | optimize", file=sys.stderr)
        return 2

    # Content manager / Good Morning Bolt
    if subcommand in MANAGER_COMMANDS or subcommand.startswith("manage"):
        env = os.environ.copy()
        env["PYTHONPATH"] = f"{CORE_DIR}" + (
            f":{env['PYTHONPATH']}" if env.get("PYTHONPATH") else ""
        )
        # Map friendly CLI to Content_Manager main() argv
        cm_args: list[str] = []
        if subcommand in ("morning", "good-morning", "goodmorning"):
            cm_args = ["morning"] + rest
        elif subcommand == "manage":
            cm_args = rest if rest else ["status"]
        elif subcommand == "store":
            # store add|list|feature-next|status|status -> store-add|…
            if not rest:
                cm_args = ["store-status"]
            else:
                action, *tail = rest
                mapping = {
                    "add": "store-add",
                    "list": "store-list",
                    "feature-next": "store-feature-next",
                    "feature": "store-feature-next",
                    "status": "store-status",
                    "verify-status": "store-status",
                }
                cm_args = [mapping.get(action, action)] + tail
        elif subcommand == "social":
            if not rest:
                cm_args = ["social-status"]
            else:
                action, *tail = rest
                mapping = {
                    "status": "social-status",
                    "package": "social-package",
                    "queue": "social-queue",
                }
                cm_args = [mapping.get(action, action)] + tail
        elif subcommand == "sponsors":
            if not rest:
                cm_args = ["sponsors-find"]
            else:
                action, *tail = rest
                mapping = {
                    "find": "sponsors-find",
                    "pitch": "sponsors-pitch",
                    "log": "sponsors-log",
                    "next": "sponsors-next",
                }
                cm_args = [mapping.get(action, action)] + tail
        elif subcommand == "business":
            if not rest:
                cm_args = ["business-lesson"]
            else:
                action, *tail = rest
                mapping = {
                    "lesson": "business-lesson",
                    "next": "business-next",
                }
                cm_args = [mapping.get(action, action)] + tail
        elif subcommand == "advance":
            cm_args = ["advance-next"] + rest
        elif subcommand in ("youtube-pkg", "yt-pkg", "youtube_pkg"):
